# Stored unified diffs carry their own required syntax (a lone space marks an
# unchanged blank line) that `git diff --check`'s trailing-whitespace rule
# cannot distinguish from real hygiene issues — and that syntax cannot be
# edited away without breaking `git apply`/`patch` on the file. Suppress the
# check on the patch's own bytes rather than mangling content required for
# the patch to remain applicable (#3318 review).
*.patch -whitespace
*.diff -whitespace
